  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 1.0,
    "cls_id": "CB07310",
    "sub_id": "43130",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": null,
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": null,
    "course_pol_en": "Important  rules:\n1. All graduate students are expected to attend to every talk in this semester.\n2. Students who are not able to attend to a seminar talk must provide reasons (justifications) by sending  emails or finding the instructor at his office.\n3. Every graduate Student must write the report and submit it, after each talk and  within 1 to 5 days.\n4. The report can be written in English (preference) or in Chinese.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": "This course will use a bilingal interaction method ( English and Chinese). The invited Speaker are free to  use English or Chinese. Thus, students should be flexible.\nIt is a good habit for students to ask questions to the speaker. It shows that students have interest in the topic\nAgain, attendance is required.\nThe instructor will take the students's attendance records of each talk",
    "ais_meno": null,
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>Students are expected to abide by the rules of good conduct. They should try to avoid all bad manners including lying, cheating, unexcused absences, rudeness, etc. Plagiarism cannot be tolerated when writing the report for each seminar talk.&quot;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>學生應遵守良好行為規範，包括避免說謊、作弊、無故缺席、粗魯等不良行為。在撰寫每次研討會報告時，絕不容忍抄襲行為。</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "Y"
  },
